    starterCode: "def update_kv_cache(cached_keys: list[list[float]], cached_values: list[list[float]], new_key: list[float], new_value: list[float], window_size: int | None = None) -> dict:\n    \"\"\"Append new key and value vectors to the inference KV cache.\n    \n    Args:\n        cached_keys: Existing sequence of key vectors.\n        cached_values: Existing sequence of value vectors.\n        new_key: New key vector to append.\n        new_value: New value vector to append.\n        window_size: Optional maximum sliding window length.\n    Returns:\n        dict with 'keys', 'values', 'seq_len', and 'evicted_count'.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Your implementation here\n    pass\n",
    mission: "Maintain autoregressive key and value states during incremental decoding with optional sliding window eviction.",
    taskDescription: "Implement `update_kv_cache(cached_keys, cached_values, new_key, new_value, window_size=None)`. Verify that `len(new_key) == len(new_value)` and that their dimensions match existing cached entries (if any). Append `new_key` to `cached_keys` and `new_value` to `cached_values`. If `window_size` is specified, retain only the most recent `window_size` vectors, evicting older entries from the front. If `window_size <= 0`, raise `ValueError`. Return a dict containing `keys`, `values`, `seq_len` (int), and `evicted_count` (int).",
    libraryPolicyText: "Libraries allowed · Pure Python earns +10 bonus XP",
