    starterCode: "def compute_inference_arithmetic_intensity(batch_size: int, seq_len: int, num_layers: int, hidden_dim: int, bytes_per_param: int = 2) -> dict:\n    \"\"\"Compute operational intensity for prefill and decode execution phases.\n    \n    Args:\n        batch_size: Number of concurrent sequences.\n        seq_len: Prompt length or current context length.\n        num_layers: Number of transformer decoder layers.\n        hidden_dim: Model hidden dimensionality.\n        bytes_per_param: Precision storage size in bytes (2 for FP16/BF16).\n    Returns:\n        dict with FLOPs and arithmetic intensities (FLOPs/byte).\n    \"\"\"\n    # Your implementation here\n    pass\n",
    mission: "Distinguish between compute-bound prefill and memory-bandwidth-bound decode phases using arithmetic intensity.",
    taskDescription: "Implement `compute_inference_arithmetic_intensity(batch_size, seq_len, num_layers, hidden_dim, bytes_per_param=2)`. Assume standard transformer with $N_{params} = 12 \times \text{num\_layers} \times \text{hidden\_dim}^2$. For prefill: $\text{FLOPs} = 2 \times N_{params} \times \text{seq\_len} \times \text{batch\_size}$, reading weights once. For decode: $\text{FLOPs} = 2 \times N_{params} \times \text{batch\_size}$, reading weights and KV cache ($2 \times \text{num\_layers} \times \text{batch\_size} \times \text{seq\_len} \times \text{hidden\_dim} \times \text{bytes\_per\_param}$). Compute arithmetic intensities (FLOPs / bytes), rounded to 2 decimal places. Raise `ValueError` on non-positive arguments.",
