    starterCode: "def verify_speculative_tree(tree_nodes: list[dict], target_greedy_tokens: dict[str, int]) -> dict:\n    \"\"\"Verify speculative draft tokens organized as a prefix tree.\n    \n    Args:\n        tree_nodes: List of dicts with 'node_id', 'parent_id', and 'token_id'.\n        target_greedy_tokens: Dict mapping node_id string -> target model next token.\n    Returns:\n        dict with 'accepted_path_token_ids', 'num_accepted', and 'best_leaf_id'.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Your implementation here\n    pass\n",
    mission: "Traverse and verify branching speculative candidate trees to maximize token acceptance rates.",
    taskDescription: "Implement `verify_speculative_tree(tree_nodes, target_greedy_tokens)`. Find the root node (`parent_id is None`). A non-root node is accepted if and only if its parent was accepted AND its `token_id` equals `target_greedy_tokens[str(parent_id)]`. Traverse the tree to find the longest path of accepted nodes starting from root. Return dict containing `accepted_path_token_ids` (token IDs along the path), `num_accepted` (int), and `best_leaf_id` (node ID of the terminal node on the longest accepted path). Raise `ValueError` if tree has no root.",
