    starterCode: "def calculate_kv_cache_memory(num_layers: int, seq_len: int, batch_size: int, hidden_dim: int, num_query_heads: int, num_kv_heads: int, dtype_bytes: int = 2) -> dict:\n    \"\"\"Calculate KV cache memory footprint across MHA, GQA, and MQA attention variants.\n    \n    Args:\n        num_layers: Number of transformer decoder layers.\n        seq_len: Active context sequence length.\n        batch_size: Number of concurrent batch sequences.\n        hidden_dim: Total model hidden dimension.\n        num_query_heads: Number of attention query heads.\n        num_kv_heads: Number of key/value heads (1 for MQA, intermediate for GQA).\n        dtype_bytes: Storage size per floating-point number (2 for FP16).\n    Returns:\n        dict with 'total_kv_bytes', 'mha_baseline_bytes', 'memory_savings_percent', and 'bytes_per_token_all_layers'.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Your implementation here\n    pass\n",
    mission: "Quantify KV cache memory savings enabled by Grouped-Query Attention (GQA) and Multi-Query Attention (MQA).",
    taskDescription: "Implement `calculate_kv_cache_memory(num_layers, seq_len, batch_size, hidden_dim, num_query_heads, num_kv_heads, dtype_bytes=2)`. Compute head dimension $d_k = \text{hidden\_dim} / \text{num\_query\_heads}$. KV elements per token across all layers is $2 \times \text{num\_layers} \times \text{num\_kv\_heads} \times d_k$. Total cache bytes is elements $\times \text{batch\_size} \times \text{seq\_len} \times \text{dtype\_bytes}$. Compute baseline MHA cache size where $\text{num\_kv\_heads} = \text{num\_query\_heads}$. Calculate `memory_savings_percent` as $(1.0 - \text{total\_kv\_bytes} / \text{mha\_baseline}) \times 100.0$, rounded to 2 decimal places. Raise `ValueError` if arguments are non-positive or if dimensions are not cleanly divisible.",
