    starterCode: "def radix_prefix_cache_lookup(tree: dict, prompt_tokens: list[int]) -> dict:\n    \"\"\"Traverse a Radix Tree KV cache to find the longest reusable prompt prefix.\n    \n    Args:\n        tree: Dict mapping node_id string -> {'token_seq': list[int], 'children': list[int], 'kv_slot_indices': list[int]}.\n        prompt_tokens: Incoming prompt token sequence.\n    Returns:\n        dict with 'matched_token_count', 'reusable_kv_slots', and 'remaining_prompt_tokens'.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Your implementation here\n    pass\n",
    mission: "Reuse precomputed KV caches across shared system prompts and multi-turn dialogues using Radix Attention.",
    taskDescription: "Implement `radix_prefix_cache_lookup(tree, prompt_tokens)`. Start from the root node (`'0'`). At each node, search its `children` for a child node whose `token_seq` exactly matches the prefix of the current unmatched prompt tokens. If found, accumulate its `token_seq` length to `matched_token_count`, append its `kv_slot_indices` to `reusable_kv_slots`, advance the prompt search position, and continue from that child. Stop when no matching child edge exists. Return dict containing `matched_token_count`, `reusable_kv_slots`, and `remaining_prompt_tokens`.",
