    functionSignature: "compute_sentence_attribution(claim_sentences: list[str], source_documents: list[str], n_gram_size: int = 2, threshold: float = 0.3) -> dict",
    starterCode: "def compute_sentence_attribution(claim_sentences: list[str], source_documents: list[str], n_gram_size: int = 2, threshold: float = 0.3) -> dict:\n    \"\"\"Evaluate grounding of claim sentences against source documents using word n-gram recall.\n    \n    Args:\n        claim_sentences: Generated sentences to verify.\n        source_documents: Ground-truth reference passages.\n        n_gram_size: Length of word tuples for overlap evaluation.\n        threshold: Minimum overlap ratio for a sentence to be considered grounded.\n    Returns:\n        Dict with 'grounded_ratio', 'sentence_scores', and 'unsupported_sentences'.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Your implementation here\n    pass\n",
    mission: "Detect ungrounded hallucinations by evaluating word n-gram overlap between generated claim sentences and retrieved source passages.",
    taskDescription: "Implement `compute_sentence_attribution(claim_sentences, source_documents, n_gram_size=2, threshold=0.3)`. Extract lowercase word tokens using `\w+`. For each sentence in `claim_sentences`, compute its set of word n-grams of size `n_gram_size` (or all words if sentence has fewer than `n_gram_size` words). Calculate recall as `len(sentence_ngrams & source_ngrams) / len(sentence_ngrams)`. Sentence is grounded if `recall >= threshold`. Return `{'grounded_ratio': ratio, 'sentence_scores': list[dict], 'unsupported_sentences': list[str]}` with scores rounded to 4 decimals. If `claim_sentences` is empty, return `{'grounded_ratio': 1.0, 'sentence_scores': [], 'unsupported_sentences': []}`.",
